        <mxCell id="p2_footer" value="&lt;b&gt;Key points&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;① The infrastructure L4 Load Balancer forwards TCP 443; Caddy owns ACME/TLS and targets only the dedicated WAFs. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ② One in-house WAF per Coder restricts selected product functions before proxying to its Coder. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ③ Browser, add-on, CLI, and agent channels follow the same Caddy → WAF → Coder path. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ④ The infrastructure TLS Load Balancer terminates TLS for other products; Certis manages its certificate. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; ⑤ HAProxy enforces Basic Auth for Flower and Prometheus." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0F172A;strokeColor=#0F172A;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontSize=16;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=22;spacingRight=22;spacingTop=12;spacingBottom=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="920" width="1800" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
